# Python virtualenvs
.venv/
venv/

# The Phase 1 SQLite ledger and its WAL sidecars. Local spend data — never committed,
# and it would conflict on every merge anyway.
meter.db
meter.db-wal
meter.db-shm
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# WildChat splits ARE committed (~1MB, ODC-BY). Regenerating them means paging the
# HuggingFace rows API, which rate-limited us at 747 rows, so a lost split is hours
# of waiting rather than a re-run. Committing also pins the exact train/val/test
# partition, which is what makes accuracy numbers comparable across sessions.
# The same applies to data/templated/ — those are 200 calls of real money.

# The dashboard's own DATABASE_URL. Same secret as the root .env, different pooler port.
dashboard/.env.local
